Edrobot wrote:
> I almost never get far in the Gnomish Mines, so today I am going to
> try going somewhat down in the main branch first.
>
> Is that wise?

Yes, it can be wise.

A few points:
Whether the level is lit or not makes a huge difference.  You can
stand on the stairs and let them come to you a lot of the time, but
thrown weapons can interfere with that idea.
How tough your pet is makes a huge difference.  Let your dog/cat
become a large one and they can clear most mine levels easily.
You can do a few more levels in the main dungeon and come back--it's
not necessarily a "Mines now or Sokoban first" decision.  You can find
the mine entrance, do a couple levels in main, and still come back and
do the mines before sokoban.
Alignment and race matter.  Being a neutral gnome makes the mines a
lot easier than being a chaotic elf.

I usually do the mines as soon as one of the following applies:
1. 50 hp
2. 0 AC
3. I have a light source and something around 3 AC/35 hp.
4. Good enough missile skills and supplies to take down beasties at a
range
5. Lit first level and #4 (so I can clear the first level and improve
my AC).

But those aren't hard and fast; a good reliable method of E or
nastiness (a bad bones level in the main branch) might send me in
earlier, among other things.  A real desire for daggers or mithril
might do likewise if I'm able to camp around the up stairs and bail in
a crisis.

It is possible, though not high percentage (the best players might
pull it off 80% of the time or so) to do the mines at XL1 with few
improvements if you're good with the pet and play smart (dropping E
like crazy when needed, running, using choke points/stairs, etc).



